# Targeted line-ending policy for the citable release tree.
#
# final_release/checksums.json records a SHA-256 per file, computed over the bytes
# on disk. Without an explicit policy those bytes depend on the checkout platform:
# with core.autocrlf=true the working tree receives CRLF while the blob holds LF,
# so 75 of the 99 recorded hashes did not reproduce on an LF checkout. Pinning the
# text in this tree to LF makes the manifest hold on every platform.
#
# Scope is deliberately narrow. Nothing outside final_release/ is byte-verified,
# so the rest of the repository is left to the user's core.autocrlf setting.

final_release/**             text eol=lf
final_release/**/*.png       binary
